The rewrite makes two changes and keeps behavior the same:

- **One type lookup:** `GetType()` is called once and the masked base-type index is reused for both table lookups.
- **Fast path:** when the base-type size equals `sizeof(T)`, the element is copied with a single `memcpy` instead of the byte-by-byte shift/OR loop. On a little-endian host this gives the same bits, including for signed `T`. Other sizes still use the original loop.

```cpp
template <typename T>
T FieldBase::GetValue(const FIT_UINT8 fieldArrayIndex) const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 typeNum = GetType() & FIT_BASE_TYPE_NUM_MASK;
    const FIT_UINT8 size = baseTypeSizes[typeNum];
    if (fieldArrayIndex >= (FIT_UINT8)values.size())
    {
        return *reinterpret_cast<const T*>(baseTypeInvalids[typeNum]);
    }

    const FIT_BYTE* p = values.data() + (static_cast<size_t>(fieldArrayIndex) * size);

    if (size == sizeof(T))
    {
        T rv;
        std::memcpy(&rv, p, sizeof(T));
        return rv;
    }

    T rv = 0;

    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++)
    {
        rv |= static_cast<T>(p[i]) << (i * 8);
    }

    return rv;
}
```

